The Command Design Pattern is a behavioral design pattern that turns a request into a separate object.

This lets you:
Parameterize objects with requests
Queue or log requests
Support undo/redo operations
Decouple sender and receiver

🧠 Real-Life Example
Think of a TV remote:
You press a button (Invoker)
The remote sends a command
The TV (Receiver) performs the action
The remote doesn’t know how the TV turns on — it just triggers the command.